    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Pi is an irrational number that is conjectured to be a rich number, meaning it is believed to contain every possible finite sequence of digits.<br><br>Given a natural number <var>N</var>, the program must determine the index of the decimal place where <var>N</var> first appears. Indexing is 1-based, starting from the digit immediately after the decimal point.<br><br>Pi = 3.14159265358979323846264338327950288419716939937510 (first 50 digits after the decimal point)</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong>  A natural number <var>N</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer representing the starting index at which <var>N</var> can be first found in PI.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; <var>N</var>&le; 100000<br><var>N</var> is guaranteed to appear within the first 50 digits of pi after the decimal point.<br><var>N</var> does not contain leading zeros.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">1</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">1</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
